{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_162620_dfe38e", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Email 1\nSubject: Your Q1 budget decision and a cloud-first alternative\n\nMorgan,\n\nWith your budget closing in Q1, you need a fleet option that fits your cloud-first team. Many engineering firms rely on cloud workstations, but your engineers still need reliable local compute for AI on drawings and simulations when site connectivity fails.\n\nThe Aurora 14 AI Workstation is built for this. It runs open-weight language models up to 30 billion parameters on-device when paired with 64 GB of memory, and it handles professional CAD and simulation tasks locally.\n\nCan I show you how the Aurora 14 fits your fleet cost model?\n\nReply to this email to schedule a 15-minute discussion.\n\n---\n\nEmail 2\nSubject: Cloud-first, but with local power\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour team is already cloud-first, so buying powerful laptops may seem redundant. The Aurora 14 does not replace cloud desktops. It augments them by providing local compute when connectivity is unreliable on site.\n\nKey facts from the spec:\n- Helix H9 AI processor with 60 TOPS NPU for on-device AI inference\n- 16 GB dedicated graphics memory for professional applications\n- Up to 11 hours of local video playback with Wi-Fi off\n- 14-inch OLED display for detailed CAD and drawing review\n\nThis gives engineers productivity on-site without adding a separate cloud bill.\n\nAre you open to a brief fleet cost review?\n\nReply to this email to schedule a 15-minute discussion.\n\n---\n\nEmail 3\nSubject: Q1 budget decision for the Aurora 14\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour Q1 budget closes soon. The Aurora 14 is available in Q4, so you can secure it before the fiscal year-end decision point.\n\nThe Aurora 14 ships with Windows 11 Pro and includes:\n- 3-year on-site, next-business-day service\n- TPM 2.0, fingerprint reader, and IR camera for security\n- Self-healing BIOS for fleet manageability\n- Two Thunderbolt 5 ports for docking and peripherals\n\nThis delivers predictable service and security across your fleet.\n\nCan I schedule a 15-minute meeting to finalize your Q1 decision?\n\nReply to this email to schedule a 15-minute discussion.", "tokens": {"input": 847, "output": 485, "total": 5151, "cache_read": 3819, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 61849, "timestamp": 1790810842082}